<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Liu Fang</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 605</span> · <a href="/centuries/6th-century">6th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Liu Fang was a general of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sui-dynasty">Sui dynasty</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>. In 602 he led an army into the Red River delta, where <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ly-phat-tu">Ly Phat Tu</a>, ruler of the Early Ly dynasty, surrendered, returning northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vietnam">Vietnam</a> to Chinese rule. In 605 he invaded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/champa">Champa</a> and sacked its capital, but he died of illness during the return march.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/liu-fang.jpg" alt="Liu Fang" width="320" height="579" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: FSIM09 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Liu_Fang.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
